-- lib/typed-language.cub — the paper's complete intrinsically typed expression language of §5.1
-- (docs/hyperactivity.cub, “A complete intrinsically typed expression language”, “Interpretation by
-- structural recursion”, “The substitution theorem”) as code: simple types with Byte, Unit, ×, +, ⇒
-- and contexts, variables vz and vs, the typed terms, environments and lookup, the interpretation by
-- structural recursion, renaming and weakening, substitution with its lift under binders, and the
-- semantic substitution environment evalEnv, and the binder law and the substitution theorem stated
-- as types (tl-binder-law, tl-substitution-theorem). Their proofs are not here: a function defined by
-- elimination of these indexed families, applied to a constructor, reduces through a transport along
-- the constructor's index path, and the machine's transport along a constant line is a path to the
-- identity (transportRefl), not a reduction; so each equation needs those transports carried, or the
-- presentation of lib/nbe.cub, whose typed codes carry their meanings in their indices.
-- Terms and variables are indexed by a context and a type (Var(Γ, A), Tm(Γ, A)); a context's tail
-- and head (tl-tail, tl-head) state the binder lifts at every index.
import "core.hypercubical"
import "xor-language.hypercubical"
import "structure.hypercubical"
